# Context

## Background
The stress gate ran C1, C2, and C3 in one job with
timeout-minutes: 420. GitHub cancels every job at 360 minutes, so
that budget was unreachable. Hosted-runner throughput drifted: the
job took 3 h 07 m on 2026-10-27 (same commit as 2026-10-29), 5 h 43 m
on 2026-10-28 with C3 at 291 min, then hit the 6 h cap and was
cancelled on 2026-10-29 and 2026-10-30, cutting all three corpora.

## Why This Way
Splitting uses only the documented MARGIN_BENCH_FULL_* switches;
ci/run-tier.sh keeps its defaults. C3 gets 350 min so the workflow
timeout fires before the platform cancel and the annotation names
the right cause. If C3 alone outgrows 350 min, the next lever is a
smaller nightly C3 scale or a larger runner, not a longer budget.

## Gotchas
- Job names changed ("Full-scale benchmark corpora" became
  "… C1 C2" and "… C3"); anything matching on job names must follow.
- A dev machine measured C3 full at ~51 min (19 days earlier); the
  291-350 min figures are shared-runner reality, not regression.
